answer:
At the time of filing a registration application for a new biological product or a biological product, the requesting company must submit a single process containing the following documents:

*   Registration petition forms FP1 and FP2, duly completed [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Original copy of the proof of payment of the health surveillance inspection fee, duly authenticated and/or stamped by the bank, or proof of exemption, when applicable [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Declaration of the company's size (economic capacity) [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Copy of the Company's Operating License and/or Sanitary Permit [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Copy of the Company's Authorization Certificate or its publication in the Official Gazette (DOU) [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Copy of the updated Technical Responsibility Certificate, issued by the Regional Pharmacy Council, proving that the requesting company and/or manufacturer has the assistance of a pharmacist qualified for that purpose [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Technical justification for the product registration [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Copy of the Good Manufacturing Practices Certificate (CBPF) issued by Anvisa for all manufacturers of the active ingredient, bulk biological product, biological product in its primary packaging, finished biological product, diluent, and adjuvant [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30].

For biological products developed via the comparability pathway, additional documentation is required, including reports on the biological product, declarations regarding the comparator product, information on the expression system, molecule comparison, and stability study reports [RDC 55/2010, Art. 43]. For biotechnological products, specific information regarding master and working cell banks and the characterization of the active substance must also be presented [RDC 55/2010, Art. 34].

According to Art. 31 of RDC 55/2010, the technical report required at the time of the registration protocol for a new biological product or biological product must include the following information:

*   Name and address of the manufacturer and the storage location of the cell bank [RDC 55/2010, Art. 31];
*   Name and address of all manufacturers of the active ingredient, the bulk biological product, the biological product in its primary packaging, the finished biological product, the diluent, and the adjuvant [RDC 55/2010, Art. 31];
*   Name and address of the issuer of the batch release certificate for the finished product [RDC 55/2010, Art. 31];
*   General data about the product, including:
    *   Pharmaceutical form and presentation [RDC 55/2010, Art. 31];
    *   Complete composition of the formulation, with all components specified by their technical names and synonyms according to the Brazilian Common Denomination (DCB), International Common Denomination (DCI), or Chemical Abstracts Service (CAS) denomination, indicating the units of measurement used [RDC 55/2010, Art. 31];
    *   Functions of each substance in the formula [RDC 55/2010, Art. 31];
    *   Route(s) of administration [RDC 55/2010, Art. 31];
    *   Instructions for use, when applicable [RDC 55/2010, Art. 31];
    *   Indications, purpose, or intended use [RDC 55/2010, Art. 31];
    *   Contraindications [RDC 55/2010, Art. 31];
    *   Side effects [RDC 55/2010, Art. 31];
    *   Adverse reactions [RDC 55/2010, Art. 31];
    *   Restrictions or precautions to be considered [RDC 55/2010, Art. 31];
    *   Precautions and warnings [RDC 55/2010, Art. 31];
    *   Drug and food interactions [RDC 55/2010, Art. 31].
